All angles are right angles.
What is the area of this figure, in $\text{km}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,3);
\draw (1.4,0.8) rectangle (3.4,1.8);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$4\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (2.4,0.8) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (3.4,1.3) {$1\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A rectangular sign has a rectangular hole cut through it.
What is the area of the sign that remains, in $\text{m}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.36]
\draw (0,0) -- (12,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$12\text{ mm}$};
\draw (12,0) -- (12,5) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$5\text{ mm}$};
\draw (12,5) -- (6,9);
\draw (6,9) -- (0,5);
\draw (0,5) -- (0,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,5) -- (12,5);
\draw[dashed] (6,5) -- (6,9) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$4\text{ mm}$};
\draw (6,5.6) -- (6.6,5.6) -- (6.6,5);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The figure is a rectangle with a triangle on top.
What is its area, in $\text{mm}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.3]
\draw (0,0) -- (15,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\draw (15,0) -- (15,6);
\draw (15,6) -- (10,10);
\draw (10,10) -- (0,10);
\draw (0,10) -- (0,0) node[midway,left,font=\small] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw[dashed] (15,6) -- (15,10) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw[dashed] (15,10) -- (10,10) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A triangular corner has been cut from a rectangle.
What is the area of the figure that remains, in $\text{cm}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.36]
\draw (0,0) -- (12,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\draw (12,0) -- (12,3) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\draw (12,3) -- (8,3) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (8,3) -- (8,6) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\draw (8,6) -- (4,6) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (4,6) -- (4,9) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\draw (4,9) -- (0,9) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (0,9) -- (0,0) node[midway,left,font=\small] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
All angles are right angles.
What is the area of this staircase, in $\text{cm}^2$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.75]
\draw (2,0) -- (5,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw (5,0) -- (5,2) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (5,2) -- (7,2);
\draw (7,2) -- (7,5);
\draw (7,5) -- (5,5);
\draw (5,5) -- (5,7);
\draw (5,7) -- (2,7);
\draw (2,7) -- (2,5);
\draw (2,5) -- (0,5);
\draw (0,5) -- (0,2);
\draw (0,2) -- (2,2);
\draw (2,2) -- (2,0);
\draw[thin] (0,2) -- (0,-1.2);
\draw[thin] (7,2) -- (7,-1.2);
\draw[<->] (0,-1) -- (7,-1) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$7\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
This figure is formed from a square. All angles are right angles and the four corner pieces removed are identical squares of side $2\text{ m}$.
What is the area of this figure, in $\text{m}^2$?
